    "id": "item_20",
    "tool": "save_domain_judgment",
    "arguments": {
      "trial_id": "kang25-recovery-2020",
      "domain_id": "domain:selection",
      "expected_revision": 4,
      "answers": [
        {
          "question_id": "sq:selection:prespecified-analysis",
          "answer": "probably_yes",
          "bases": [
            {
              "evidence": "eh_24073ec1c815a7cd",
              "role": "direct_support"
            },
            {
              "evidence": "eh_b1530cb7162d3c93",
              "role": "context"
            },
            {
              "evidence": "eh_4a4db61b21438e7b",
              "role": "direct_support"
            },
            {
              "evidence": "eh_f807c3fc5b52e369",
              "role": "context"
            },
            {
              "evidence": "eh_45882a0e281c9667",
              "role": "context"
            },
            {
              "evidence": "eh_122bbac5f99a027b",
              "role": "context"
            }
          ],
          "justification": "The captured protocol identifies the trial and is dated 1 February 2010; its contents state that it includes the original SAP as the only version. That plan specifies the primary composite and ITT analysis, Kaplan\u2013Meier/log-rank methods, and Cox hazard ratios. The protocol\u2019s July 2014 revision summary concerns study timeline and exercise-testing eligibility, not analysis; recruitment began July 2010. The report presents the matching primary composite/ITT result and says the authors vouch for fidelity to protocol. This supports, by inference, a prespecified applicable plan before unblinded data were available. However, the approved HR is reported as Fine\u2013Gray, a method not listed in the SAP, and the captured sources do not date investigators\u2019 access to unblinded outcomes; thus not a definitive yes.",
          "unknowns": [
            "When investigators first had access to unblinded outcome data.",
            "Whether the Fine\u2013Gray primary HR method was specified outside the captured original SAP."
          ],
          "counterevidence": [
            {
              "evidence": [
                "eh_4a4db61b21438e7b",
                "eh_45882a0e281c9667",
                "eh_122bbac5f99a027b"
              ],
              "implication": "The SAP specifies Cox HRs, while the article identifies the reported primary HR as Fine\u2013Gray; this leaves a method correspondence gap, although the article also reports Cox analyses and does not explain the choice as result-driven."
            }
          ],
          "limitations": [
            {
              "premise": "The captured protocol/SAP does not establish when investigators accessed unblinded results, and it does not show whether the reported Fine\u2013Gray HR was prespecified elsewhere.",
              "stopping_rationale": "Inspected the full protocol chronology, change summary, original SAP, and main-report analysis/result passages; registry retrieval is unavailable at normal intake. The support for early prespecification is therefore inferential, not conclusive."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "question_id": "sq:selection:multiple-measurements",
          "answer": "no",
          "bases": [
            {
              "evidence": "eh_fb45d1def9f691b8",
              "role": "direct_support"
            },
            {
              "evidence": "eh_45882a0e281c9667",
              "role": "context"
            },
            {
              "evidence": "eh_122bbac5f99a027b",
              "role": "direct_support"
            },
            {
              "evidence": "eh_24073ec1c815a7cd",
              "role": "context"
            }
          ],
          "justification": "The protocol specifies one primary composite endpoint\u2014operative mortality or cardiovascular mortality over the entire follow-up (minimum four years)\u2014with its component definitions. The approved result is that same composite and follow-up target, and the report presents the primary endpoint result plus cumulative-incidence information at follow-up times; the inspected sources do not indicate that one among multiple eligible primary-domain measurements was selectively fully reported because of its result. Other specified secondary endpoints are distinct outcomes, not alternative measurements of this primary composite.",
          "unknowns": [],
          "counterevidence": []
        },
        {
          "question_id": "sq:selection:multiple-analyses",
          "answer": "no_information",
          "bases": [
            {
              "evidence": "eh_4a4db61b21438e7b",
              "role": "direct_support"
            },
            {
              "evidence": "eh_45882a0e281c9667",
              "role": "direct_support"
            },
            {
              "evidence": "eh_122bbac5f99a027b",
              "role": "direct_support"
            },
            {
              "evidence": "eh_19262bce4c37b1af",
              "role": "context"
            }
          ],
          "justification": "The SAP specifies ITT, Kaplan\u2013Meier/log-rank and Cox HR analyses. The report describes stratified Cox with Firth correction, Kaplan\u2013Meier/Gray, a Fine\u2013Gray competing-risk analysis for the primary endpoint, and per-protocol/subgroup analyses; its primary HR is specifically attributed to Fine\u2013Gray. Thus multiple analyses are possible and at least some method detail differs from the SAP. Neither the captured report nor protocol establishes that the reported estimate was chosen because it was favorable or that competing analyses were withheld for their results. Multiplicity/mismatch alone cannot support probable selection; the basis for any choice remains unresolved.",
          "unknowns": [
            "Whether the Fine\u2013Gray analysis and other reported analyses were prespecified or supplementary, and whether analyses/results were withheld because of their findings."
          ],
          "counterevidence": [
            {
              "evidence": [
                "eh_4a4db61b21438e7b",
                "eh_45882a0e281c9667",
                "eh_122bbac5f99a027b"
              ],
              "implication": "The plan/report method difference and several reported methods establish multiplicity or possible deviation, but do not establish result-driven selection; the report provides more than one primary-endpoint analysis/result summary."
            }
          ],
          "limitations": [
            {
              "premise": "The captured Sources do not explain why the Fine\u2013Gray estimate was used for the reported primary HR or establish whether eligible alternative analyses were withheld based on results.",
              "stopping_rationale": "Inspected the original SAP, the final-protocol analysis passage, the protocol change summary, and main-report statistical methods and primary-endpoint results. The registry is unavailable at intake; remaining result-dependence cannot be resolved from these captured passages."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "outcome": "success"
